                    "type": "markdown",
                    "title": "Usage",
                    "content": "```python\nimport joblib\nimport numpy as np\n\nmodel = joblib.load('california_housing_model.joblib')\n\nX = np.array([[\n    8.33,    # median_income (~$83,300)\n    41.0,    # house_age (years)\n    6.98,    # avg_rooms\n    1.02,    # avg_bedrooms\n    322.0,   # population\n    2.56,    # avg_occupancy\n    37.88,   # latitude\n    -122.23  # longitude\n]])\n\nprice = model.predict(X)[0]\nprint(f'Predicted: ${price:.2f} hundred k')\n```"
